{"number": 51, "text": "                     Exercises\n\n\n            22.1\n                     Match the words  on the left with their collocations on the right.\n                     1 set         additives\n                     2 food        food\n                     3 junk        produce\n                     4 ready       menu\n                     5 fresh       meals\n\n            22.2\n                     Complete  these sentences using the collocations from exercise 22.1 to fill the gaps.\n                                                         such as artificial flavours and colouring can cause allergies.\n                     2                                   may be unhealthy, but it’s quick and easy and fills you up.\n                     3 People who  don’t have much time to cook often buy ...                             from\n                       the supermarket.\n                     4 It’s always better to DUY                                instead of canned or frozen foods.\n                     5 The\n                                                             is usually cheaper than ordering dishes separately in a\n                       restaurant.\n\n            22.3\n                     Read these remarks  by different people, then answer the questions.\n                      Logan:   I’ve got some cheese and milk. Is there a fridge here | could put them in?\n                     Connor:  |       hungry! | can’t believe it!\n                       Layla:  I’ve been sick and my stomach is aching. Must be something | ate.\n                     Michael: No  matter how much | eat, | always want more.\n                     Scarlett: All these vegetables have been grown without any chemicals at all.\n                       Bella: {| always enjoy my food and look forward to it.\n\n\n                      1 Who  has organic food?\n\n                      2 Who  has an insatiable appetite?\n\n                      3 Who  has perishable food?\n\n                      4 Who  has a healthy appetite?\n\n                      5 Who  has food poisoning?\n\n                      6 Who  is dying of hunger?\n\n\n            22.4\n                    Replace  the underlined words with suitable collocations from the opposite page.\n                    1  Foods which are changed or treated as part of an industrial operation may damage our health in\n                       the long term.\n                    2  Some  people always have three full, satisfying meals a day, but | prefer a large breakfast and then\n                       a small meal around midday and a more sizeable meal in the evening.\n                    3  There are some overpriced restaurants in the city centre, but down at the beach, there are some\n                       nice, not too expensively priced ones.\n                    4  On my  birthday my parents took me out for a big, good meal. They wanted to go for a very high\n                       quality meal but | said I’d prefer something more ordinary.\n                    5  Iced tea is a drink that cools you and makes you feel less tired on a hot day, and is probably better\n                       for you than non-alcoholic drinks such as cola or lemonade.\n                    6  Let me take you out to dinner on your birthday. Or would you prefer a meal prepared at home?\n                       | could make dinner for you at my place.\n\n\n                                                                     English Collocations in Use Intermediate    49", "char_count": 3473, "mean_conf": 91.58, "word_count": 421, "words": [{"text": "22.1", "x0": 250, "y0": 354, "x1": 351, "y1": 391, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "22.2", "x0": 246, "y0": 731, "x1": 349, "y1": 767, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "22.3", "x0": 244, "y0": 1216, "x1": 347, "y1": 1253, "conf": 95, "bold": true}, {"text": "22.4", "x0": 239, "y0": 2341, "x1": 344, "y1": 2378, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "Exer